======================================================================
EXPERIMENT 2: device softmax determinism on REAL 7B logits (saved npy)
    ntl_sds03_p1_native.npy = lm_head logits, sds_03.pdf:molecular_weight p1 native
======================================================================
argmax id=2753; best Yes id=9454 ('Yes'); gap(Yes vs argmax) fp64 = -23.187500
true P(Yes) fp64-from-fp16-logits = 8.507397e-11   (NO float32 exp underflow at play: 8.5e-11 >> 1.18e-38)
device softmax run0: P(Yes)=np.float32(0.0) P(No)=np.float32(1.0) n_zero=152057/152064; log_softmax: yes=np.float32(-inf)
device softmax run1: P(Yes)=np.float32(0.0) P(No)=np.float32(1.0) n_zero=152057/152064; log_softmax: yes=np.float32(-inf)
-> device fp16 softmax: deterministic per array, but EXP IS fp16:
   any non-argmax token with true prob < ~2.98e-8..5.96e-8 (fp16 subnormal shoulder) -> 0.0 -> logprob = -inf
   frozen code: mx.exp(-inf) = 0.0 -> score = 0.0/(0.0+1) = 0.0 EXACTLY
   NOTE: spec hypothesis P(Yes)<1e-38 float32-exp underflow is NOT the mechanism;
   the collapse happens EARLIER, inside fp16 device exp of the softmax.

